  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc, 46.4% F1), which is a weak baseline. We have zero information about whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. This is the most critical unknown: if image features are uninformative, the entire multimodal branch (~36 configs) is low-value, and we should focus on improving the RNA side. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest possible probe of image-modality informativeness. It uses a standard, well-validated encoder (ResNet-50) in the simplest profile setting, so any performance difference from config_001 can be attributed to the modality/encoder rather than confounding complexity from aggregation or fusion. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a tight budget, resolving whether the second modality is useful at all is the highest-leverage question. A strong image-only result would justify investing in multimodal fusion configs; a weak result would redirect effort toward better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. It also establishes a second single-modality baseline, making future multimodal comparisons interpretable (does fusion beat the best single modality?). Changing only the modality from RNA to image keeps the comparison maximally informative with minimal confounds."
}

